Taking another step in mastering containerized deployments! Here’s how I streamlined the process: 

🔹 Cloned the project from GitHub 
🔹 Logged into AWS Elastic Container Registry (ECR) 
🔹 Built and tagged the Docker image 
🔹 Pushed the image to AWS ECR 
🔹 Spun up a container from the hosted image 

🛠 Key Commands Used: 

# Clone the repository 
git clone <git repository> 

# Login to ECR 
aws ecr get-login-password --region us-east-1 | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin 

# Build the Docker image 
docker build -t myimage2:v2 2128 tween_agency 

# Tag the image 
docker tag myimage2:v2 <image path> 

# Push to ECR 
docker push <image path> 

# Run the container 
docker run -itd --name container -p 1234:80 <image path> 

